        "id": 250866,
        "name": "",
        "username": "skywhale",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/skywhale/{size}/5248_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-02-20T17:39:39.326Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Is this Definitive Edition?</p>\n<p>I believe it is the same answer either way, but for sure in Definitive Edition you would no longer trigger any effects from the power, as it is no longer in play. And in Definitive Edition, card effects not in play cannot affect play.</p>\n<p>Edit: Just tested this out for EE with VG Writhe (Umbral Siphon power deals 2 separate instances of damage), Mister Fixer (can destroy Umbral Siphon with his power), and Captain Cosmic (can give Fixer Dynamic Siphon, which allows him to use his power between the two instances of damage from Umbral Siphon). Umbral Siphon dealt the first instance of damage to Dynamic Siphon, which allowed Fixer to destroy Umbral Siphon, and then the second instance of damage was not dealt (lots of siphoning going on).</p>\n<p>So in both editions, the power would end when the card that contains the power is destroyed.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2023-02-20T17:54:48.229Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
