        "read": false,
        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "I thought both editions were clear that cards remain in play while resolving *their own* destruction, which is why, for instance, Mountainous Carapace still grants Akash'Bhuta -1 damage or why Bee Bot works the way it does. But if those kinds of effects are not happening then something destroying the card interrupts whatever else it was doing. (Famous example: End of Days/Bee Bot)",
